  "description": "The meme trivializes and normalizes acts of terrorism by framing suicide bombing as a mundane 'job' one comes home from, juxtaposed with a domestic reaction. This can desensitize viewers to the real-world consequences and moral weight of such acts, potentially contributing to a culture that minimizes or trivializes violence against civilians. It also reinforces harmful stereotypes by linking terrorism to a specific gendered domestic trope (the 'wife look'), which can perpetuate Islamophobic narratives.",
